Theorem RL-1: Realization rule signatures — RL-1 through RL-34 + RL-13 confirmation-of-removal

  Preconditions:
    - Realization rules govern logical ownership events, mutation-isolation
      obligations, donor/recipient credit transfer, backend-neutral
      allocation-fact freezing, target-plan capability validation, logical
      event refinement, ordering barriers, backend projection of AIMS facts,
      and borrow inference per Annex E §AIMS.
    - Transforming RL rules have signature
      ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction. Fact-freezing and projection
      rules instead return AllocationFacts or prove Satisfies; they do not
      smuggle a physical target choice through that transformation signature.
    - 37 active RL theorems (RL-1 through RL-34 minus RL-13-REMOVED, plus
      RL-11a / RL-14a / RL-15a / RL-18a sub-rules) per the section
      inventory table (line 108)
    - RL-13 was REMOVED from Annex E §AIMS (same root cause as DP-10)
    - RL-31 (type-level disjointness) requires cross-call-site
      provenance-summary parameter per Annex E §AIMS RL-31

  Soundness property:
    Common transformation signature where a rule rewrites realization IR:

      RL-N-transform : ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction

    Backend-neutral allocation seam:

      freeze : ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> AllocationFacts
      validate : AllocationFacts x ExtentClass x LayoutCapabilities -> Satisfies

    Logical ownership-event cluster (RL-1 through RL-5):
      RL-1 owner-credit event when an owned value gains a simultaneous owner
      RL-2 release event at last use of an owned value or scope exit;
             excludes ownership-transferring uses; includes UNUSED-owned
             definitional cleanup for Dead/Absent
      RL-3 event pairs elided when the lattice proves them unnecessary
             (via DP-2, DP-3, DP-7)
      RL-4 edge-specific release events on CFG edges with Jump-arg exemption
      RL-5 dead-at-entry cleanup for Owned non-scalar block parameters with
             Cardinality = absent

    Mutation-isolation cluster (RL-6 through RL-10):
      RL-6 ProvenUnique mutation preserves the same logical identity
      RL-7 RequiresSharingObservation chooses between preserving identity and
             isolating the mutation from aliases
      RL-8 ProvenShared mutation requires isolation before mutation
      RL-9 explicit and compact observation forms have identical logical
             mutation outcomes
      RL-10 disjoint field mutation needs no aggregate isolation when
             field-disjoint borrows prove non-interference
             (DP-5 field-aware disjointness; SetTag conservatively blocks)

    Donor/recipient credit-transfer cluster (RL-11 through RL-12, minus
    RL-13-REMOVED):
      RL-11 same-block transfer: an eligible donor relinquishes one storage
             credit that the recipient acquires under conditions (a, b, c)
      RL-11a MaybeShared donors require a sharing observation; the isolated
             outcome transfers credit and the shared outcome creates a fresh
             recipient credit without consuming the donor
      RL-12 cross-block transfer requires dominance / post-dominance, the
             same innermost loop header, and no-throw constraints

    Allocation-fact freeze cluster (RL-14 through RL-17):
      RL-14 Locality derives a logical LifetimeBound; it never chooses stack,
             arena, region, or managed placement.
      RL-14a CleanupObligation preserves exact release-event, drop-plan,
             traversal-order, normal-exit, unwind-exit, and lifetime-end identity.
      RL-15 ExtentClass is representation-owned projection input, separate
             from AllocationFacts.
      RL-15a ArgEscaping freezes a nonempty exact CallerExtent containing
             stable call-site identity and borrow/share/transfer protocol;
             missing caller evidence becomes Unknown.
      RL-16 missing or conflicting evidence freezes conservative defaults:
             Lifetime Unknown, Owner Unbounded, Thread PotentiallyShared,
             Visibility Unknown, and unknown logical event obligations.
      RL-17 OwnerBound is a dynamic upper bound; bounded straight-line
             additional-credit sites contribute N extra owners, while loops,
             global reachability, or external credit creation force Unbounded
             even for local-unique input.

    Target-projection capability cluster (RL-18 through RL-18a):
      RL-18 VmLayoutPlan and CompiledLayoutPlan are admissible only with a
             proof of Satisfies over lifetime, repr extent, owner capacity,
             exact ownership-observation and cleanup events, unwind coverage, thread
             reachability, and visibility. Capability refinement separately
             preserves external-contract identity.
      RL-18a VM and compiled plans may choose different physical mechanisms,
             but validated plans erase to the same exact AIMS logical trace.

    Thread-reachability cluster (RL-19 through RL-21):
      RL-19 Locality plus call-graph boundary evidence freezes Confined or
             PotentiallyShared; Unknown is PotentiallyShared.
      RL-20 PotentiallyShared requires a shared-safe capability, while
             Confined admits either confined-specialized or shared-safe
             mechanisms; AIMS does not select an atomicity implementation.
      RL-21 a whole-program no-thread-boundary proof freezes all values as
             Confined, still leaving mechanism selection to each target.

    KnownSafe + logical event-refinement cluster (RL-22 through RL-26):
      RL-22 KnownSafe pair elimination when a logical owner credit is proven
             outstanding across the candidate pair (no physical counter premise)
      RL-23 KnownSafe flag propagation at joins (AND across predecessors)
      RL-24 bidirectional dataflow identifies matching
             (owner-credit, release) pairs
             across blocks
      RL-25 pair eliminable when KnownSafe = true OR both paths safe AND
             no CFG hazard
      RL-26 event motion forbidden across observable barriers per Annex E
             §AIMS RL-26 (ownership-transferring or sharing-observing calls;
             mutation-sharing observations; aggregate mutation affecting v)

    Event-ordering barriers cluster (RL-27 through RL-28):
      RL-27 calls require selected pending logical events to be ordered before
             entry when the callee may transfer ownership or observe sharing
      RL-28 unknown callees conservatively order all pending logical events
             before entry

    Backend-neutral AIMS fact export (RL-29 through RL-31):
      RL-29 FreshSelfAllocationFacts from IC-4 returns_fresh_self_alloc;
             passthrough and consumed-storage results remain unproven; a
             compiled backend may separately project this fact into a
             target-specific direct-pointer ABI attribute
      RL-30 MemoryAccessFact from IC-3 + IC-5 + realized operations;
             ReadOnly proves no writes but permits all reads;
             may_throw or may_write_inaccessible forces ReadWrite; a compiled
             backend may project generic read-only metadata, never a stronger
             claim than the conservative AIMS fact
      RL-31 neutral disjoint-Borrowed-parameter facts; target alias metadata
             is a separate projection; cross-call-site provenance is required
             (cross-function alias-disjointness proof from borrow_sources +
              project_alias_sources at each call site) — VF-2 (b) consumes
             this; the burden-prototype C5 CRITICAL criterion

    Borrow inference cluster (RL-32 through RL-34):
      RL-32 all non-scalar parameters initialize Borrowed; fixpoint promotes
             to Owned based on demand
      RL-33 projection propagation: projected field Owned -> source promoted
             Owned
      RL-34 tail call preservation: every handoff or release is ordered before
             the tail call; an Owned callee receives ownership, while a
             Borrowed tail call is valid only when the caller's release
             obligation is already discharged

    RL-13 confirmation-of-removal entry:

      RL-13 — Construct + Once does NOT imply one logical owner at death (REMOVED)

      Removed in: Annex E §AIMS RL-13 removal note
        (same root cause as DP-10)

      Root cause: one use may store the value into a data structure and create
        another logical owner; Construct + Cardinality=Once alone does not
        guarantee exactly one logical owner at death.

      Subsumed by:
        - Uniqueness dimension (§AIMS §3.4) as direct source of truth for
          reuse eligibility
        - DP-6 + RL-11 + RL-12 reuse-candidate gating via Uniqueness

      No theorem skeleton to discharge; this is a CONFIRMATION entry only.

